<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · island</p><h1 class="enc-title">Vanua Balavu</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Vanua Balavu is the largest island of the northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lau-islands">Lau group</a> in eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fiji">Fiji</a>, a long, irregular island of limestone and volcanic rock with sheltered bays. In the 19th century its village of Lomaloma became the seat of the Tongan noble <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/enele-maafu">Enele Maʻafu</a> and of the Tovata confederacy that he formed with Fijian chiefs in 1867.</p></div>
